        "commit": {
          "author": {
            "name": "Sergey Biryukov",
            "email": "sergeybiryukov@git.wordpress.org",
            "date": "2026-10-21T20:40:01Z"
          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "Sergey Biryukov",
            "email": "sergeybiryukov@git.wordpress.org",
            "date": "2026-10-21T20:40:01Z"
          },
          "message": "Tests: Use the null coalescing operators in the test suite.\n\nReplaces `isset()` and `array_key_exists()` ternaries that return the tested value or a fallback of `null` or `''` with the null coalescing operator (`??`), and self-referencing `$x = $x ?? $y` assignments with the null coalescing assignment operator (`??=`).\n\n**Why this is safe**\n\n- `??` and `isset()` test the same condition, so the fallback is used in exactly the same cases.\n- `array_key_exists()` and `??` only differ for a key that exists with a `null` value. Every converted `array_key_exists()` site falls back to `null`, so both forms return `null` in that case as well.\n- `??=` requires PHP 7.4, which is already the minimum supported version.\n- No behavior change; this is test-only code.\n\nDeveloped in https://github.com/WordPress/wordpress-develop/pull/14616.\n\nFollow-up to r63609, r63633.\n\nProps Soean, huzaifaalmesbah.\nSee #65819.\n\ngit-svn-id: https://develop.svn.wordpress.org/trunk@64675 602fd350-edb4-49c9-b593-d223f7449a82",
